  "disclosures": "Non-blind: the flow_24/flow_32 values and the quadratic structure were known before the run.  The direction was selected as the max-min of the flow_24/flow_32 predictions: a selected line, not a random draw.  Lattice commensurability confound: the design lattice (0.025 m) equals the flow_32 spacing, flow_24 is coarser, flow_40/48 finer; resolution and lattice alignment change together, and any convergence is that of this interpolated-lattice body only.  The 3e-5 N floor is nominal, the 1e-5 N guard band is the scale of the fit residuals, not a noise measurement.  Multigrid-depth confound: WaterLily 1.8.0 builds 4, 6, 4 and 5 multigrid levels on flow_24, flow_32, flow_40 and flow_48 and caps the pressure solve at 32 iterations (tol 1e-4), so part of any flow_24/flow_32 difference may be pressure-solver convergence rather than resolution; the Poisson statistics above are descriptive, reported not gating.  The verdict uses the fit including the -1.25 mm reverse state (a report-only probe for the gates); the forward-only G_max is reported without classification; with 3 dof per fit one outlier is partly absorbed, so read G_max together with the acceptance emulation.  Not claimed: grid independence, physical or Stage V downforce, a gradient, optimizer behaviour.  No GRIDRES-01 result alone supports a GRID-01 amendment.",
